# Supplemental astrometry for 83 formerly unassociated color targets (2026-10-18).
# gaia_dr3: EDR3/DR3 source_id; distance_pc: parsecs, without a precision cut.
# EDR3_WD: CDS J/MNRAS/508/3877/maincat, distance = 1000 / Plx (mas).
# DR3: https://gea.esac.esa.int/tap-server/tap/sync, distance = 1000 / parallax (mas).
# SIMBAD_G107-70_system: system parallax 83.484 mas; resolved Gaia sources lack parallaxes.
# Optional Gaia G/BP/RP magnitudes and proper motions (mas/yr) accompany each added target.
# Full WDJ positions remain at J2000; metadata tokens are not aliases.
# Hollands et al. (2026), Any colour you like: the diverse chromaticities of white dwarfs.
# DOI: 10.1093/rasti/rzag069. Tables C3-C6, CC BY 4.0.
# 239 published color entries: C3=15, C4=36, C5=36, C6=152; 236 coordinate identities.
# Paper coordinate label, full WDJ identifier, disc-averaged sRGB, table/method, verified aliases.
# Paper labels are J2000, not B1950 WD identifiers. Aliases never set astrometry or magnitudes.
# alternative: retained overlapping result; earlier calibrated spectrum/fitted model takes priority.
# unresolved_component=N: separate model for an unresolved binary component; no automatic assignment.
# C6 notes: a=pure-He assumption; b=unresolved binary; c=non-Gaia parameters;
# d=UV parameters with assumed DA atmosphere; e=observed SDSS spectrum.
# The conflicted printed alias WD2150+591 is excluded from association (two coordinate identities).
